Z||000000||Lou Christopher||08-17-2000||11:45 AM||||Starters. As most of you know I purchased a 84 Se with a 350 chev. auto trans archie kit.  I have spent the last coulple of months working on it. Lastest problem is that it eats flex plates. Previous owner told me he replace 2. i just replaced flex plate and TC.  Starter still does not engage starter properly ( no amount of shimming helps.  I rationalized that the starter was designed for 153 tooth chev and the Fiero flex has 142 and that was the problem.  Called Powermaster and Tilton without good results.  Whent to see my local stater remanufacturer and he said the fiero and chev pinion gears are the same and showed them to me.  Does anyone have any experience with this problem?<BR>Would appreciate any thoughts.<BR>                     Lou<P><BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||08-17-2000||11:53 AM||||Tooth pitch could do this.... Do you have any pictures of a dead plate you can post?<P>You could have one or both of 2 other porblems.<P>1. starter not pushing bendix far enough out into flex plate gear. if the tranny is mounted with an adaptor plate that's a real posibility.<P>2. starter not engaging teeth deep enough. The bendixn and plate are only hitting tips of teeth. In this case the starter needs to be milled off then shimmed if need be. This would happen if the Fiero plate is slightly smaller in diameter than the one the V8 would normally take. (This is a real posibility since you said the fiero plate has fewer teeth.)||||reg||1
